<title>GERMANY: Most on EMI council support ERM membership for EMU.</title>
<headline>Most on EMI council support ERM membership for EMU.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A clear majority of the European Monetary Institute council support the need for membership of the Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) as a requirement for inclusion in the planned currency union.</p>
<p>&quot;Regarding the Treaty provision of membership of the ERM, there is a strong majority position within the EMI Council that the requirement of ERM membership applies,&quot; the report said in a copy of the report on European Monetary Union convergence obtained from the Bundesbank.</p>
<p>The EMI said that a minority takes the view that exchange rate stability based on underlying fundamentals is more important than the institutional setting within which stability is achieved.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
